347
00:35:05,663 --> 00:35:08,193
Redis is our cache layer.

348
00:35:08,653 --> 00:35:12,303
It provides high speed data storage
for frequently accessed data

349
00:35:20,991 --> 00:35:23,361
We use Redis 7 Alpine.

350
00:35:24,101 --> 00:35:29,391
This is the official Redis
image based on the Alpine Linux.

351
00:35:29,911 --> 00:35:35,991
Alpine is a minimal Linux distribution
that keeps the image small and secure.

352
00:35:37,231 --> 00:35:41,911
The command section passes
argument to Redis server.

353
00:35:41,911 --> 00:35:48,761
We use the append-only set to
yes to enable AOF persistence.

354
00:35:50,331 --> 00:35:54,521
AOF writes every write
operation to a log file.

355
00:35:55,021 --> 00:35:58,451
This ensures that data
survives container restarts.

356
00:35:59,631 --> 00:36:03,661
The requirepass flag
sets the Redis password.

357
00:36:04,131 --> 00:36:04,151
The

358
00:36:07,381 --> 00:36:12,191
