must be set in the .env file.

359
00:36:12,271 --> 00:36:16,111
Without a password,
Redis will be insecure.

360
00:36:18,691 --> 00:36:25,061
The next flag is the maximum memory
flag, which sets the memory limits.

361
00:36:25,511 --> 00:36:33,171
The default size is five one two MB.
When memory is full, Redis evicts

362
00:36:33,171 --> 00:36:37,871
keys using the policy specified
by the maximum memory policy.

363
00:36:38,961 --> 00:36:44,722
We use the allkeys-lru
as the eviction policy.

364
00:36:45,711 --> 00:36:49,411
LRU stands for least recently used.

365
00:36:50,191 --> 00:36:56,301
When memory is full, Redis exists
the least recently used keys first.

366
00:36:57,031 --> 00:36:59,381
This is the default behavior for caching.

367
00:37:00,541 --> 00:37:03,051
The next flag is the tcp-keepalive.

368
00:37:08,772 --> 00:37:11,961
This flag enables the tcp-keepalive.

369
00:37:12,352 --> 00:37:18,072
This prevents connections from being
closed by firewalls due to inactivity.

370
00:37:18,731 --> 00:37:24,731
The value sixty means that keepalive
packets are sent every sixty seconds.

371
00:37:33,193 --> 00:37:38,153
We map port six three seven nine
from the container to the host.

