questions and the agent response.

490
00:50:49,107 --> 00:50:52,787
Both are texts which can
handle any length of text.

491
00:50:53,817 --> 00:51:00,557
Analysis style can be one of
analysts or executive or risk.

492
00:51:00,917 --> 00:51:05,457
This controls the styles of the
analysis performed by the agent.

493
00:51:05,997 --> 00:51:09,517
The check constraint ensures that
only value types are inserted

494
00:51:25,213 --> 00:51:29,623
The agent type identifies which
agent produced the response.

495
00:51:30,053 --> 00:51:35,933
This could be financial agent, the query
agent, or the query engine fallback.

496
00:51:36,923 --> 00:51:41,803
Source chunk ID is a
PostgreSQL array of UUIDs.

497
00:51:42,253 --> 00:51:46,773
It stores the chunk IDs that
were used to generate the answer.

498
00:51:48,423 --> 00:51:51,513
This enables the source attribution.

499
00:51:52,543 --> 00:51:58,213
The latency in milliseconds stores
the query latency in milliseconds.

500
00:51:58,323 --> 00:52:04,073
This is used for performance monitoring
and service level objective tracking.


