00:33:50,132 --> 00:33:51,742
We define the removed API.

434
00:33:52,872 --> 00:33:55,932
These are APIs removed in Kubernetes

435
00:34:01,938 --> 00:34:05,248
These API versions are deprecated.

436
00:34:05,808 --> 00:34:09,008
They will not work on
newer Kubernetes cluster.

437
00:34:09,658 --> 00:34:13,268
Using them leads to failed up-upgrades.

438
00:34:14,498 --> 00:34:17,938
We write the rule that denies removed API.

439
00:34:19,128 --> 00:34:23,918
If a manifest uses a removed
API, the policies deny it.

440
00:34:24,758 --> 00:34:27,658
This prevents failed upgrade.

441
00:34:28,258 --> 00:34:30,388
Now let's write the HPA rule.

442
00:34:30,858 --> 00:34:37,988
It requires HPA to use auto-scaling
version two Autoscaling version

443
00:34:37,998 --> 00:34:41,068
two supports multiple metrics.

444
00:34:41,408 --> 00:34:43,978
Autoscaling version one is limited to CPU.

445
00:34:45,038 --> 00:34:48,978
This rule enforces the
better API for autoscaling.

446
00:34:49,487 --> 00:34:52,148
Now let's create the Terraform policy.

447
00:34:52,758 --> 00:34:57,438
Inside of the Rego, we create
the terraform_policy.rego.

448
00:34:58,438 --> 00:35:01,728
The Terraform policy validates
infrastructure as code.

449
00:35:02,468 --> 00:35:04,618
It catches security issues.

450
00:35:05,017 --> 00:35:06,667
We write the S3 rule.

451
00:35:07,407 --> 00:35:12,887
It requires S3 buckets to
block public access This rule

452
00:35:13,057 --> 00:35:16,497
checks the public access block.

453
00:35:17,597 --> 00:35:20,548
If it's not configured, the policy denies.

454
00:35:21,038 --> 00:35:25,108
This prevents accidental
public exposure of S3 buckets.

455
00:35:26,108 --> 00:35:31,458
The RestrictsPublicBucket setting
is an additional security control.

456
00:35:32,678 --> 00:35:38,598
It ensures that buckets aren't
publicly accessible even if

457
00:35:38,598 --> 00:35:39,328
the ACL is misconfigured.

458
00:35:40,328 --> 00:35:42,468
Now we write the RDS rule.

459
00:35:43,188 --> 00:35:45,528
It requires RDS encryption

460
00:35:46,528 --> 00:35:50,318
That is, financial data
must be encrypted at rest.

461
00:35:51,158 --> 00:35:53,458
This rule enforces that requirements.

462
00:35:53,968 --> 00:35:57,528
No unencrypted RDS instance are allowed.

463
00:35:59,088 --> 00:36:02,768
RDS instances must be publicly accessible.

464
00:36:03,648 --> 00:36:07,188
This prevent direct database
access from the internet.

465
00:36:07,928 --> 00:36:11,028
All access should go
through the application.

