00:29:07,015 --> 00:29:10,735
This  is  where  we  will  build
the  network  security  layer

372
00:29:10,735 --> 00:29:13,395
for  our  financial  AI  agents.

373
00:29:14,195 --> 00:29:18,195
We  have  deployed  the  application
to  EKS,  but  right  now

374
00:29:18,195 --> 00:29:20,635
pods  can  talk  to  anything.

375
00:29:21,675 --> 00:29:22,675
There  are  no  restrictions.

376
00:29:23,175 --> 00:29:24,995
This  is  a  security  risk.

377
00:29:25,745 --> 00:29:28,165
Think  of  it  like  an  office  building.

378
00:29:28,925 --> 00:29:32,345
Without  security,  anyone
can  walk  into  any  room.

379
00:29:37,545 --> 00:29:41,725
However,  the  security
officers  won't  allow  that.

380
00:29:49,525 --> 00:29:54,065
We  need  to  implement  a
zero -trust  networking.

381
00:29:54,785 --> 00:29:58,245
Zero -trust  means  never
trust,  always  verify.

382
00:29:59,045 --> 00:30:02,765
That  is,  every  connection
must  be  explicitly  allowed.

383
00:30:03,805 --> 00:30:05,385
Cilium  is  our  tool  for  this.

384
00:30:06,005 --> 00:30:11,925
It  provides  the  eBPF -based
networking,  security,  and

385
00:30:11,925 --> 00:30:13,565
observability  for  Kubernetes.

386
00:30:13,565 --> 00:30:19,425
Let  me  show  you  why
Cilium  is  special.

387
00:30:19,940 --> 00:30:23,840
Traditional  Kubernetes  Network
policies  use  IP  tables.

388
00:30:24,780 --> 00:30:27,400
They  work  at  Layer  3  and  Layer  4.

389
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:29,700
They  don't  understand  HTTP.

390
00:30:30,900 --> 00:30:33,020
Seleum  uses  eBPF.

391
00:30:33,460 --> 00:30:35,980
It  works  at  the  kernel  level.

392
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:41,280
It  can  enforce  Layer  3,  Layer
4,  and  Layer  7  policies.

393
00:30:41,770 --> 00:30:45,450
It  can  see  HTTP  method  and  paths.

394
00:30:46,290 --> 00:30:47,230
This  is  important.

395
00:30:48,050 --> 00:30:54,590
We  want  to  allow  the  API  to  call
the  agent,  but  on  posts  that  is

396
00:30:54,590 --> 00:30:58,110
slash  infer,  not  on  any  other  paths.

